# 03 — Fix and prevent

<!-- GEN: Why: a root-cause fix at the right layer with a regression test is the only fix that stays fixed; green-washing removes the protection that found the bug. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->

<!-- GEN: Rules D6–D9, D11 with the workspace's sibling skills and gates. -->

## Fix

1. **Regression test first** (per {{unit_testing_link}}): it fails now for the reason you found.
2. **Smallest change at the right layer** (per {{clean_architecture_link}}), inside the approved scope. {{edit_rule}} <!-- GEN: e.g. "Run GitNexus impact on the symbol before editing; warn on HIGH/CRITICAL." -->
3. Rerun the regression test, then the affected suite ({{ref_05}}).
4. Remove every temporary print/log/breakpoint you added.

## Never

| Tempting shortcut | Why it is forbidden |
|---|---|
| Edit, skip or `xfail` the failing test | Hides the defect and removes the check that found it |
| Fake fallback, broad `catch`/`except`, default value on failure | Turns a loud failure into silent wrong data |
| Loosen a type or an assertion | Lets the same bug through next time |
| `sleep` / retry to make a race pass | The race is still there, only rarer |
| Disable a lint rule or gate | Removes protection for everyone |

